--- A builtin with a row in the table is one runtime function that both
--- modes call, failing as the row says (docs/bug-classes.md §4). A
--- calendar of a zone that does not exist is an error value of kind
--- 'time', as the spec lists it: the compiled program printed to stderr
--- and answered an empty map. An invalid pattern is an error value of kind
--- 'regex', as find[]'s is: the interpreter answered one where the compiled
--- program stopped, and both typed matches[] a bool. A negative count is
--- the misuse that stops.
c = calendar[0.0, tz = 'UTC']
log[c['year']]
bad = calendar[0.0, tz = 'Nowhere/Nothing']
log[bad.ok]
log[bad.kind]
log[parse_time['2026-01-02 03:04:05', tz = 'UTC']]
m = moment[2026, 1, 2, tz = 'Nowhere/Nothing']
log[m.ok]
log[m.kind]
log[repeat['ab', 3]]
log[matches['crow', 'c..w']]
log[sub['crow', 'o', '0']]
bad_pattern = matches['crow', '(unclosed']
log[bad_pattern.ok]
log[bad_pattern.kind]
log[bad_pattern.reason]
log[sub['crow', '[', 'x'].kind]
log[repeat['ab', 0 - len[[1]]]]
log['not reached']
